Explanation: every binary package SuperMox rebuilds from patches/ (scripts/
  apply-patches.sh) is pinned out of Proxmox's repository outright: their
  builds are systemd-based, so apt upgrade must never replace ours. The
  +supermoxN version suffix apply-patches.sh adds to those components'
  changelogs already makes their build look like a downgrade; this -1 pin is
  the hard guarantee, because apt ignores a version with a negative pin
  entirely. The list is generated by scripts/supermox-pin-packages.sh from
  the patched trees' debian/control files, and tests/test-supermox-ve.sh
  fails the gate when it drifts.
